// optim/ — optimizers and learning-rate schedules.
//
// Sits on core. The schedules compare a loss against the previous best and
// decide the next learning rate; the optimizers step parameter arrays in
// place, carrying their own state (m, v, step count). None of that needs to
// know what kind of thing is being trained, which is why this package was the
// one place in the tree that could be split without first untangling anything
// else.
//
// It imports nn/ for `LinearParam` and `Conv2dParam` -- not to run them, only
// because the *layout-specialised* update wrappers (`adam_update_linear`,
// `adam_update_conv2d`) hand back a fresh parameter block of that exact type.
//
// That import used to point the other way. layer_norm.mbt and batch_norm2d.mbt
// reached `@optim.sqrtf` to normalise a tensor, so nn/ depended on optim/ for a
// square root and the two could not be separated at all. Moving sqrtf, cosf and
// sinf into core/ is what broke the cycle.
import {
  "riantr/snn_mbt/core",
  "riantr/snn_mbt/nn",
}
